\n• Critique sessions\n\nLesson Plan:\n\nWeek 1 – Introduction to Watercolor Techniques (2 sessions)\n\nSession 1:\n• Introduce students to the basic concepts of watercolor painting.\n• Explain the basic materials of watercolor painting, including paints, paper, brushes, and water.\n• Discuss the importance of color theory.\n• Demonstrate basic brush strokes and techniques.\n• Allow students to experiment with the materials and techniques.\n\nSession 2:\n• Introduce students to the concept of pigment mixing.\n• Discuss color schemes and harmonies.\n• Demonstrate color mixing techniques and color charts.\n• Allow students to experiment with the materials and techniques.\n\nWeek 2 – Watercolor Painting Techniques (2 sessions)\n\nSession 1:\n• Introduce students to the concept of wet-on-wet painting.\n• Demonstrate the process.\n• Allow students to experiment with the technique.\n• Have students paint a simple abstract composition using the technique.\n\nSession 2:\n• Introduce students to the concept of dry-brush painting.\n• Demonstrate the process.\n• Allow students to experiment with the technique.\n• Have students paint a simple still life composition using the technique.\n\nWeek 3 – Watercolor Paintings and Conceptualization (3 sessions)\n\nSession 1:\n• Review color theory and pigment mixing.\n• Discuss the importance of personal expression and creativity in art.\n• Allow students to brainstorm ideas for their painting.\n• Have students sketch out their painting concept.\n\nSession 2:\n• Introduce the concept of focal point and compositional balance.\n• Allow students to refine th","tokens":["<","|","im","_","start","|>","system","\n","You"," are"," a"," helpful"," assistant",".<","|","im","_","end","|>","\n","<","|","im","_","start","|>","user","\n","Write"," a"," comprehensive"," lesson"," plan"," for"," teaching"," high"," school"," students"," the"," basics"," of"," water","color"," painting",","," including"," color"," theory",","," brush"," strokes",","," 